A field the new version removes from a struct an each body writes: it is
reported at that struct, and the drop the help offers goes inside it, named
as the element of the list the body builds.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	items: [...{
		meta: {
			owner: string
			note:  string
		}
	}]
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	items: [...{
		meta: {
			owner: string
		}
	}]
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		items: _each(v0_0.items, {
			meta: {
				owner: _item.meta.owner
			}
		})
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	items: [...{
		meta: {
			owner: string
		}
	}]
}
-- out/error --
error[E0347]: v0.0 declares meta.note and v1.0 does not, and nothing maps it
  --> history/1.0.thema:13:4
   |
13 |             meta: {
   |             ^^^^
   |
   = help: write <field>: _item.meta.note to move it, or add note: _drop to v1_0.items[].meta
